The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    public function deleteMultiple($keys): bool
    {
        $this->ensureValidType($keys);

        foreach ($keys as $key) {
            $result = $this->delete($key);
            if ($result === false) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `Cake\Test\TestCase\Cache\CacheTest::testDeleteManyPartialFailure`:
            
```php
    public function testDeleteManyPartialFailure(): void
    {
        $this->_configCache();
        $data = [
            'App.exists' => 'yes',
            'App.exists2' => 'yes',
        ];
        Cache::writeMany($data, 'tests');

        $result = Cache::deleteMany(['App.exists', 'App.noExists', 'App.exists2'], 'tests');
        $this->assertFalse($result);

        $this->assertNull(Cache::read('App.exists', 'tests'));
        $this->assertNull(Cache::read('App.exists2', 'tests'));
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Failed asserting that 'yes' is null.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
    public function deleteMultiple($keys): bool
    {
        $this->ensureValidType($keys);

        $allDeleted = true;
        foreach ($keys as $key) {
            $result = $this->delete($key);
            if ($result === false) {
                $allDeleted = false;
            }
        }

        return $allDeleted;
    }
```
